l`. To watch the test fail, I set line 2 back to `\"Products\"` for one run.\n- It failed where it should: `Expected: \"Product Catalog\"`, `Actual: \"Products\"` at `CatalogTitleE2eTest.cs:20`. That means the shop started and the browser read the title; the failure is the assertion, not a setup error.\n- I then set the title back to `\"Product Catalog\"`. `git diff` shows the view as the build left it, and `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` is clean.\n\n**What `tests.md` records:** one criterion mapped to that test, the two test files, and notes on the red run, your decision, and why there are no unit or integration tests.\n\n**Two things to watch:**\n- In the working tree the view already says \"Product Catalog\", so this test is green now. When the gate runs `--stage test`, it will see a passing test that was recorded red earlier and whose expectation changed on a decision. Whether it counts `catalogue-title-01` for that is up to the gate: the decision is recorded under the build stage, not the test stage.\n- The test's display name must also appear as a scenario title in `../dca-sample-specification/scenarios.md` and in the Java suite. I haven't checked either, because they're outside this stage's inputs.","ttft_ms":2714,"type":"result","duration_ms":92247,"uuid":"883cb3c5-6fbf-4e5f-a717-e6f89d943e87","ttft_stream_ms":1846,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1847,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
